The '''eighth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' began on 29 August 2017,<ref name="Launch2017">{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-40949537|title=Great British Bake Off: BBC moves rival cooking show in scheduling spat|work=BBC News|date=16 August 2017|access-date=17 August 2017}}</ref> with this being the first of ''The Great British Bake Off'' to be broadcast on [[Channel 4]], after the production company Love Productions moved the show from [[BBC One]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-37353262 |title=Why did The Great British Bake Off move to Channel 4? |first= David |last=Sillito|date=13 September 2016 |work=BBC }}</ref> It is the first series for new hosts [[Noel Fielding]] and [[Sandi Toksvig]], and new judge [[Prue Leith]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2017/aug/29/the-great-british-bake-off-2017-channel-4-episode-one-live|title= The Great British Bake Off 2017, episode one – as it happened|date=29 August 2017|work=Guardian|access-date=30 August 2017}}</ref>

This series was won by [[Sophie Faldo]], with Kate Lyon and Steven Carter-Bailey finishing as runners-up.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/0/great-british-bake-series-verdict-bake-break-channel-4-played/ |title= The Great British Bake Off series verdict: it was bake or break, but Channel 4 played a blinder|date=31 October 2017|work=The Telegraph|access-date=1 November 2017}}</ref>

