=== Episode 9: Pâtisserie (Semi-final) ===
For the semifinal signature bakes, the bakers were asked to make 24 [[Choux pastry|choux]] buns—12 must have a crunchy [[craquelin]] on top, and the other 12 must be covered with icing—in {{frac|2|1|2}} hours. For the technical challenge, which was set by Prue Leith, the bakers were tasked with a very difficult job of making 9 [[Misérable cake|Les Misérables slices]] to be done in 3 hours. For the showstopper challenge before the final, the bakers were asked to make a [[meringue]] centrepiece, containing at least two different types of meringue and a dessert element, in 4 hours and 45 minutes.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/live/2017/oct/24/great-british-bake-off-2017-semi-final-follow-it-live |title=The Great British Bake Off 2017 semi-final – as it happened|date=24 October 2017|work=Guardian|access-date=31 October 2017}}</ref>{{sticky header}}{{table alignment}}
